      "1978 model puts Y/Ca as different dominant site cations.2025 model suggests Y dominance in both and explicitly requires Canadian reinvestigation before species equivalence can be resolved. No unapproved new caysichite species curated.",
      "2025 abstract says4472 unique observed reflections; Table2 distinguishes4472 independent and3906 observed. Numerical reflection claims omitted from owner.",
      "2025 conclusion formula1 REE2.05Ca1.87 vacancy0.18 sums4.10 cation sites, while given x=.025,ysecond=.055 imply vacancy.08. Formula2 printed HCO3.21 differs2*.115=.23 from parameter set. These are bounded arithmetic checks, not corrected crystallographic models. Detailed disputed formulas not promoted to owner.",
